      "key": "cq_coverage",
      "value": {
            "1": "EDIFACTMessage (or InvoiceMessage) is composed of InvoiceMessage instances via containsMessage and hasSection; invoices are InvoiceMessage instances contained in an EDIFACTMessage.",
            "2": "Organizations involved are linked via hasOrganization (InvoiceMessage->Organization), and more specifically via RoleAssignment and involvesOrganization.",
            "3": "RoleAssignment (pivot class) links an Organization to its AgentRole within an InvoiceMessage (via hasRoleAssignment, involvesOrganization, hasAgentRole).",
            "4": "RoleAssignment with hasAgentRole=Buyer identifies the buyer organization for a given invoice.",
            "5": "Organization is linked to Address, Identifier, GlobalLocationNumber, and AgentRole through hasAddress, hasIdentifier, hasGlobalLocationNumber, and RoleAssignment; all info about organizations is available via these properties.",
            "6": "The address of the buyer is obtained by following RoleAssignment (hasAgentRole=Buyer) to the Organization, then hasAddress.",
            "7": "LineItem (in InvoiceDetailSection) is linked to Item via hasItem; items sold are instances of Item associated with LineItems of the invoice.",
            "8": "Item is linked to Price, Quantity, and other attributes via hasNetPrice, hasQuantity, etc. All info about items is accessible via these properties from LineItem.",
            "9": "Net price of items is expressed via hasNetPrice (LineItem->Price), and Price has value as a data property.",
            "10": "Invoice details are captured in InvoiceHeaderSection (reference numbers, dates, etc.), InvoiceDetailSection (line items), and InvoiceSummarySection (totals, tax).",
            "11": "Invoice amount is represented as hasInvoiceAmount (InvoiceSummarySection, xsd:decimal).",
            "12": "Invoice number is a data property (hasInvoiceNumber) of InvoiceHeaderSection.",
            "13": "Mandatory info for file format validity is modeled via SHACLConstraint, EDIFACTDirectory, and hasMandatoryIdentifier; constraints and required identifiers are captured as properties.",
            "14": "Business process assignment is modeled via hasBusinessProcess (InvoiceMessage->BusinessProcess)."
      }
}
